.TH RECHNE 1.SH NAMErechne \- a calculator, in German.SH SYNOPSIS\fBrechne\fR[\-b] expression.SH DESCRIPTION\fBrechne\fRevaluates an expression and prints the answer in decimal, hexadecimal andbinary at once.  The expression is one argument with no spaces:\fBrechne 4095+1\fR.\fRThe operators are\fB+\fR\fB\-\fR\fBx\fR(times)\fB/\fRand\fBm\fR(modulo), and\fBa\fR,\fR\fBo\fRand\fBp\fRfor AND, OR and XOR; a number after\fB$\fRis hexadecimal.\fB\-b\fRlists which bits are set..PPIts other switches decode status codes of DESIGNA's own systems.  DESIGNA VLT, UTIL 2.80..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSObc, chbase